linux-computer-use

src/lcu/motion.py contains a Python port of the cursor glyph and motion
model from maka-agent
(apps/desktop/src/renderer/computer-use-overlay/engine/cursor-engine.ts,
commit 5551d6cd1c730542d8584ef295584607f9ae4428,
https://github.com/maka-agent/maka-agent), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
Changes: translated to Python; path planning and spring integration run in
the MCP server, while the scoot/press springs run in the GTK overlay.

According to that project, the glyph outline and motion constants were
recovered from the AgentCursor in OpenAI's Codex desktop app
(SkyComputerUseService). Codex and OpenAI are trademarks of OpenAI; this
project is not affiliated with or endorsed by OpenAI.
